Q: Decltype not able to pick a template function based on its concept A: <p><code>decltype</code> rules don't play well with overloaded functions. If you add some boilerplate to get the overload set of a function, then a slight modification to <code>func</code> to take a value type can solve this:</p>
<pre><code>// Source - https://stackoverflow.com/a/46588937
// Posted by Yakk - Adam Nevraumont
// Retrieved 2026-02-18, License - CC BY-SA 3.0

#define RETURNS(...) \
  noexcept(noexcept(__VA_ARGS__)) \
  -&gt; decltype( __VA_ARGS__ ) \
  { return __VA_ARGS__; }

#define OVERLOADS_OF(...) \
  [](auto&amp;&amp;...args) \
  RETURNS( __VA_ARGS__( decltype(args)(args)... ) )
</code></pre>
<p>Now you can do:</p>
<pre><code>template&lt;auto f, class T&gt;
auto func(const T &amp;value){
    return f(value);
}

myStruct struct3 = func&lt;OVERLOADS_OF(myAbs&lt;myStruct&gt;)&gt;(struct1);
</code></pre>
